## PRD: Capability 3, Submit Request to OPF API

**Blocking question OQ-A (separate service or inside Wire Rail II)**
Resolved by the team: one fully synchronous service, Wire Rail II, with no separate submit service and no SQS. The combined Capability 10 draft reflects this and is awaiting formal approval. Stage naming (OQ-D) is to be confirmed with the PayX integration team; the current design uses WIRECLEARING / WIRECLEARING.STOP with no intermediate stage.

**FR-1, Submit to OPF API**
Same state as Capability 2 FR-1: the call is built and exercised against the WireMock stub; a real submission is blocked until FIS configures the Discover backend after the SOW. The uuid and idempotency-key (= UETR) headers are implemented.

**FR-2, Map OPF response to PayX outcome**
Proceeding. The mapping table is implemented against the stubbed responses. Two things to confirm before this is final: the stage names (WIRECLEARING versus OPFCLEARING), and the exact FIS error bodies, which FIS has promised as samples. No pain.002 or MQ outcome is consumed in Phase 1, as FIS confirmed.

**FR-3, Store OPF response against the transaction record**
Proceeding in code; not blocked by FIS. The DynamoDB table itself is not provisioned yet (table, encryption key, IAM policy and VPC endpoint are new infrastructure work on our side).

**FR-4, Return final status to PayX**
Design settled: Wire Rail II is synchronous, so the final status is the HTTP response of the Wire Rail II call itself, returned to the new PayX integration service. There is no separate status call back to PayX. The Bank Wire Rail II API contract is registered on Exchange and needs an architecture review before cyber approval; it will be shared with the PayX integration team once onboarded to non-prod. Retries stay with PayX (Arbiter replay with the same UETR).

